SM: Yeah, for privacy. But anyhow, I was happy. I loved every minute of it. I enjoyed everything. I was happy to be in the United States. I loved United States. I said, my god, why wasn't I born here? I missed all the 13 years. I was 13 when I came. And [PAUSES] I loved everything. I was just-- I was just overjoyed, happy, happy. And other people, they had complaints. And there's a fence. The fence didn't bother me. There's a fence around the camp. What did we come to another camp, you know? And a lot of complainers and-- not me. I loved everything. For one month, we were supposed to stay in the camp. A month later, they allow us to go to public schools. We went to public schools. I love public schools.

